1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
China to Europe by rail? The wheels don't fit.
I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
China's tracks are 1,435 mm. Russia's: 1,520.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,300
So at the border, the train has to stop.

4
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,600
Each carriage is lifted off its wheels.

5
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,000
Wider bogies are rolled underneath.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,400
Then it rides on into Russia and Europe.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,600
Double-tap if you never knew this.

8
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,200
It happens at Manzhouli, on the Russian border.

9
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,000
★ Expert Tip: the Trans-Manchurian to Moscow crosses right here.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,600
So: did you know the wheels change? Tell me.
